"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The preoperative PSA was elevated at 6. The surgical findings included a pathological stage of pT3a with extraprostatic extension, negative surgical margins, and no invasion of the seminal vesicles. The absence of lymph nodes removed is a factor, and the biopsy showed Gleason 3+4. Countervailing findings include the negative surgical margins and the absence of lymphovascular invasion. The lack of documented nodal sampling widens the uncertainty regarding true nodal status. The biopsy grade was documented, and the surgical pathology grade was also documented, which is relevant for comparison. Information that would revise this prognosis significantly includes the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up data prevents a definitive assessment of recurrence risk. The fixed estimated horizon is 57.04 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 34.23–79.86 months; its coverage has not been validated."
